00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:20.960 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  hey everyone its Peter Brown standing in  for freelance reviewer Jason to April  for his review of next machina next  machina is a modern revamp of Robotron  2084 in all but name and developer  housemarque even managed to collaborate  with Robotron x' creator eugene jarvis  to bring the high-quality homage to life  conceptually the two games are nearly  identical and every aspect of next  machina is appropriately chock-full of  nostalgia the gorgeously trippy graphics  feel simultaneously modern and retro and  the synth Wave soundtrack complements  the sci-fi action perfectly  [Music]  in the same vein as pac-man Championship  Edition next machina is one of the best  modernisations of a classic arcade game  that you can find its plot is brief and  to the point you're a lone hero trying  to save what remains of humanity during  a robot apocalypse the twin-stick  shooting action that defines your fight  is tight and responsive and every world  is relentlessly challenging individual  levels are small fast paced and  frequently packed with secrets to  discover MIT's the chaotic hero on robot  action and death comes instantly whether  you get hit by a lone bullet or simply  bump into a nearby enemy next machina is  pronounced difficulty is by design  harkening back to the challenge of its  arcade source material beyond advancing  through stages skillful play is rewarded  through item upgrades bonus points and a  strong sense of satisfaction from  overcoming seemingly impossible odds  next machina is hard but is also  thoroughly gratifying  [Applause]  world complete your primary objective in  each level is to destroy a number of  enemy waves before rocketing off to the  next set piece there are however  numerous secondary objectives to  consider along the way as with Robotron  there are a handful of humans haplessly  wandering around each stage rescuing  them just by touching them requires  precise timing as you must not only  protect your own hide but also defeat  enemies who are whittling away the  wandering humans health saving humans is  considered optional but it's a  relentlessly tempting and risky  distraction that you'll chase time and  time again even when you should know  better  [Music]  boss battles at the end of each world  are the biggest test throwing out dense  curtains of bullets that demand exacting  movements to avoid all are challenging  and each is drastically different from a  mechanical ape that sits atop of the  screen and throws flaming debris at you  - a giant Terminator like skull and a  hive mind boss that attacks from the  safety of a protective field adding to  the challenge boss fights follow a  series of dense enemy waves and if you  lose all your lives and end up using a  continue you have to start the process  all over again  [Music]  now you can point to dense waves of  enemies and monstrous bosses as the  reasons next machina is so hard but more  than their numbers our size is the range  of tactics enemies employ that  ultimately stress you out some  mindlessly plow toward you others will  make bee lines to humans and there are  burrowing turrets that send out waves of  exploding balls among a variety of other  robotic dangers you typically face  myriad enemy types all at once from all  directions creating a juggling act that  would be impossible to contend with if  not for your special abilities dashing  is central to surviving in next machina  harsh world as it was in-house marks  previous games resogun in Super Stardust  once activated you're invulnerable for  the duration of the lunch and your  timing has to be perfect given the small  margin for error in most levels misjudge  the duration of your - through a crowd  by a nanosecond and you'll lose a life  since there's a brief recharge period  between dashes you can't abuse it by  default either this is alleviated  somewhat if you spot and grab a triple  dash powerup but these are few and far  between and don't completely diminish  the risk of an untimely sprint in the  wrong direction  secondary weapons however are more  prevalent and can make or break you  depending on the scenario your options  include powerful lasers rockets floating  bombs or a sword for deadly close up  attacks these also require a brief pause  to recharge which reinforces the idea  that your ability to manage cooldown  meters is a critical skill and another  important layer to track during frantic  on slots you can in theory play through  next machina in under an hour  but it's eminently replayable thanks to  the number of Secrets waiting to be  found and the skills you need to hone in  order to survive and climb to the top of  the leaderboards you do have the option  of bringing a friend along but next  mocking is multiplayer is woefully  limited to local engagement zone a lack  of online play is a notable  disappointment next machina is a game  that confidently meets expectations it's  difficult intensely satisfying and  packed with enough secrets and lofty  secondary objectives to keep you and  raptured for hours  it's a classic game at heart but with  refined challenges and exacting  mechanics it feels right at home in the  modern era  [Music]

